* After our pass: continuations

Phase 4 (NOTES.md #P3). Wherever one of the tables of the other files leaves a
player to pass (the table's implicit pass, NOTES.md #C2), the auction used to
leave the system at the partner's next turn: our own pass is a trie edge only
where a history line names it. This file names it. Its default, written below
for every table that has no pass of its own, as the table's lowest-ranked call
(`{prio:-100}`, chosen exactly when no other row applies), is the simplest reading of a
partnership that has stopped: after one of us passes, and whatever the
opponents do next, the partner passes too (a `{stop}` pass, `passes.bml`). Only
the frequent opener's reopening after an overcall and responder's pass is
written out with real calls.

** The partnership stops after a pass

