** Opener's reopening after an overcall and responder's pass

Responder's pass over a one-level overcall is often a trap pass with length in
their suit (a negative double would have shown the other suits), so opener,
short in their suit, reopens with a double; opener rebids a six-card suit;
otherwise opener passes. After the reopening double responder passes for
penalty with four cards in their suit, bids notrump with a stopper, and
otherwise returns to opener's suit, which carries no requirement of its own.
The partnership then stops.

#CUT reopen-answer
P = {prio:3} 6+ hcp, 4+\Y
  #STOP
3N = {prio:2} 13+ hcp
  #STOP
2N = {prio:2} 11--12 hcp
  #STOP
\R = {prio:-1} any hand
  #STOP
#ENDCUT

1X-(1Y)-P-(P)-
D = {prio:2} 12+ hcp, 0--2Y
2X = {prio:1} 12--16 hcp, 6+X
  #STOP
P = {prio:-100} {stop} any hand

1X-(1Y)-P-(P)-D-(P)-
1N = {prio:2} 6--10 hcp
  #STOP
#PASTE reopen-answer \Y=Y \R=2X

1X-(1Y)-P-(P)-D-(any)-
P = {prio:-100} {stop} any hand

1Y-(2X)-P-(P)-
D = {prio:2} 12+ hcp, 0--2X
2Y = {prio:1} 12--16 hcp, 6+Y
  #STOP
P = {prio:-100} {stop} any hand

1Y-(2X)-P-(P)-D-(P)-
#PASTE reopen-answer \Y=X \R=2Y

1Y-(2X)-P-(P)-D-(any)-
P = {prio:-100} {stop} any hand

1X-(2Y)-P-(P)-
D = {prio:2} 12+ hcp, 0--2Y
3X = {prio:1} 12--16 hcp, 6+X
  #STOP
P = {prio:-100} {stop} any hand

1X-(2Y)-P-(P)-D-(P)-
#PASTE reopen-answer \Y=Y \R=3X

1X-(2Y)-P-(P)-D-(any)-
P = {prio:-100} {stop} any hand

** Opener after they compete over our stop (NOTES.md #P10)

The system stops let the partnership pass with any hand once one of us has passed,
whatever the opponents do. At the positions below that answer is not SAYC's, so
they get real rows; the stop pass stays as the lowest-ranked call for the rest.

*** After the negative double of a two-level overcall and their raise

Opener is no longer forced to bid. With four cards in the major the double
promised he competes (game with 17+); without a major to show over their raise of
a major, the double showed the minors and opener bids a four-card minor at the
four level with 15+; he rebids a six-card suit with 15+ (game in a major with
18+). Otherwise he passes.

1C-(2D)-D-(3D)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete-3 \M=H \s=h
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete-3 \M=S \s=s
4C = {prio:0} 15+ hcp, 6+!c
  #STOP

1C-(2H)-D-(3H)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete-3 \M=S \s=s
4C = {prio:0} 15+ hcp, 6+!c
  #STOP

1C-(2S)-D-(3S)-
4H = {prio:3} 17+ hcp, 4+!h
  #STOP
4C = {prio:0} 15+ hcp, 6+!c
  #STOP
P = {prio:-100} {stop} any hand

